crossed:
The dawn now breaks on you, the dark is over,
The sea is crossed, the longed-for port is won;
Farewell, oh, fare you well! my friend and lover.

cross:
How Jesus' blood for your redemption flows.
See him with hands out-stretcht upon the cross;
Immense compassion in his bosom glows;

crouched:
Went snuffing round my garden bound,
Or crouched by my bower wall?
With a silken leash about his neck;

crown:
Of his dead love. So be it. I preserve
That crown still,—in the drawer there! ’twas the first;
The rest are like it;—those Olympian crowns,

crow:
Slews o' Grasshoppahs a-fiddlin' lak to save dey life;
Mistah Crow, 'he call de figgers, settin' in a tree,
Huh, uh! how dose critters sasshayed was a sight to see.

crows:
So 's to hide an' view you;
Whole flocks o' camp-meetin' crows
Shoutin' hallelujah.

croaking:
Chuckling and choking,
Croaking, croaking, croaking:--
Let the beacon-fire blaze higher;

crowns:
Where saints and angels greet;
To cast our crowns with songs of love
At our Redeemer's feet.

crocodile:
While still like hungry death he fed his maw;
Till every minor crocodile being dead
And buried too, himself gorged to the full,

crowd's:
The gray train rushing bears the weary wind;
In the packed cars the fans the crowd’s breath cut,
Leaving the sick and heavy air behind.

crow's:
An' it beats ole Ned to see the way
'At the crow's feet's a-getherin' aroun' yore eyes;
Tho' it ought n't to cause me no su'prise,

crowdin:
Oh, de major man's a-swingin' of his stick,
An' de pickaninnies crowdin' roun' him thick;
In his go'geous uniform,

crost:
Play de kettle drum,
Lookin' crost de medders
Swimmin' lak a sea;

Out thaih in de night;
An' yo' cabin 's 'crost de lot:
Run, Miss Lucy, run;

cromwell:
Violet now, in veil on veil of evening
The hills across from Cromwell grow dreamy and far;
A wood-thrush is singing soft as a viol

crock:
That the next man who came should prove the scheme;
And you were he.  Jan handed you the crock.
Two whiffs!  And then the pipe was broke, and you were freed."

crockery:
My host withdrew himself apart;
Busied among his crockery,
He paid no farther heed to me.
